{#
	One module the customer could add, saying enough to decide with (XIV-140).

	**What it needs is the body of the tile now**, and that is XIV-140's own
	observation rather than a design flourish: [XIV-23] already computes it, and it
	is most of what somebody needs in order to know whether this module is a step
	they can take today. Before this the body said how many presets the module has,
	which is a number about a choice nobody has started making.

	**Every requirement is named, not only the missing ones.** "Needs Contacts and
	Orders, and you have both" is the sentence that lets somebody stop worrying;
	listing only the gaps means a tile that says nothing is a tile you still have to
	open to find out why. The missing ones carry the warning colour *and* the word,
	because a colour is not a statement and a screen reader cannot see one.

	**The buttons are the module page's buttons, under the module page's two
	grants.** Installing and committing the company to a payment are different
	authorities (§8.4.3), so `can('install', …)` and `can('buy', …)` are asked
	separately, and somebody holding neither reads a tile that is complete and
	simply does not act. A module that needs something missing gets no button at
	all rather than a disabled one, for the reason `show.html.twig` gives: a control
	that cannot be used is a question with no answer on it.

	**A price appears only where there is one** (XIV-102). See `_price.html.twig`,
	which has the argument for why free is silent.
#}
<div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-4">
	<div class="card h-100">
		<div class="card-body d-flex flex-column">
			<h3 class="h6 card-title d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-2">
				{% if offer.blueprint.icon %}
					<i class="bi bi-{{ offer.blueprint.icon }} text-body-secondary" aria-hidden="true"></i>
				{% endif %}
				<span class="me-auto">{{ offer.label }}</span>
				{#
					The price sits in the heading rather than in the body, so that a
					reader scanning a grid for "what costs money" scans one column. It
					renders nothing for a free module, which is why the card looks
					untouched for every module in this build.
				#}
				{{ include('store/_price.html.twig', {offer: offer, currency: currency, emphasis: 'small fw-semibold'}) }}
			</h3>

			{#
				They pressed the button yesterday and nothing has happened since, which
				is exactly what was supposed to happen (XIV-102). Said on the tile so
				that nobody is left wondering whether it worked.
			#}
			{% if offer.hasBeenRequested %}
				<p class="card-text mb-2">
					<span class="badge text-bg-info">{{ 'store.requested'|trans }}</span>
				</p>
			{% endif %}

			{% if offer.requirements is not empty %}
				<p class="card-text small mb-2">
					<span class="text-body-secondary">{{ 'store.requires'|trans }}</span>
					{% for requirement in offer.requirements %}
						<span class="badge {{ requirement.installed ? 'text-bg-light border' : 'text-bg-warning' }}">
							{{ requirement.label }}
							<span class="visually-hidden">({{ (requirement.installed ? 'store.installed' : 'store.not_installed')|trans }})</span>
						</span>
					{% endfor %}
				</p>
			{% endif %}

			{#
				Kept from before XIV-140 and demoted rather than dropped: how many ways
				there are to install it is a real thing to know about the decision
				ahead, and it was only ever wrong as the *only* thing the tile said.
			#}
			<p class="card-text text-body-secondary small mb-3">
				{{ 'store.preset_count'|trans({'%count%': offer.presets|length}) }}
			</p>

			<div class="mt-auto d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
				<a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" href="{{ path('store_module', {module: offer.key}) }}">
					{{ 'store.details'|trans }}
				</a>
				{% if offer.isInstallable and can('install', chrome.store) %}
					<a class="btn btn-sm btn-primary" href="{{ path('store_install', {module: offer.key}) }}">
						<i class="bi bi-download" aria-hidden="true"></i>
						{{ 'store.install'|trans }}
					</a>
				{% elseif offer.isBuyable and not offer.hasBeenRequested and can('buy', chrome.store) %}
					<a class="btn btn-sm btn-primary" href="{{ path('store_buy', {module: offer.key}) }}">
						<i class="bi bi-bag" aria-hidden="true"></i>
						{{ 'store.ask_to_buy'|trans }}
					</a>
				{% endif %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
